WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:25.000
An infant secured to a chair with a strip of cloth around his chest is tapping his hands on a table, his fingers spread.

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:31.700
He touches the table and waves his arms.

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:42.540
A small cube is placed in front of him.
He looks at the object, then looks away, then picks up the cube.

00:00:50.436 --> 00:00:56.436
He drops it, grabs for it, and then retrieves it again.

00:00:58.836 --> 00:01:04.836
The baby continues handling the cube. A second cube appears in his hand. He drops a cube on the floor more than once.

00:01:12.436 --> 00:01:18.436
A third cube is placed in front of the baby.

00:01:19.369 --> 00:01:25.369
Now baby has no cubes. He rubs his hands on the table where the cube(s) had been.

00:01:34.236 --> 00:01:44.236
A small dinner bell is placed on the table.
Baby reaches for it, picks it up, handles it, and holds it in front of his face.

00:01:55.103 --> 00:02:01.103
Now an upside down mug is placed in front of him, then taken away.

00:02:05.969 --> 00:02:11.969
Baby is lying on his back and an adult is holding a rattle just above him. He reaches for it, grabs it, waves it around.

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:35.360
Rattle is gone and adult helps baby sit up.

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:50.500
Now baby stands, with assistance.

00:03:07.736 --> 00:03:15.736
The child is back at the same table.

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:28.460
He spreads his hands across the table, then handles a cube, then two, then more, followed by the mug.

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:23.880
All objects are removed. The child examines the table, looks around, rubs his face.

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:33.840
The dinner bell is placed in front of him and he handles it, banging it against the table occasionally.

00:04:42.736 --> 00:04:52.536
An adult hand shows him how to ring it up and down.
He handles it again, mouths it, bangs it.

00:04:56.536 --> 00:05:02.536
An adult takes the bell back and demonstrates again.

00:05:08.203 --> 00:05:14.203
Now a large ring with a string attached is placed in front of the child, and he plays with it. Then a board with cut-out shapes appears.

00:05:21.403 --> 00:05:27.403
The child removes the circle shape and plays with it, perhaps trying to place it back in its correct cutout.

00:05:33.469 --> 00:05:39.469
The child is sitting up, with the rattle placed just out of reach. He rolls around, reaching for the rattle, and eventually grasps it.

00:06:11.703 --> 00:06:17.703
The child is sitting up again, facing in the other direction.

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:47.040
The toddler is back at the same table, handling different numbers of cubes and a mug. An adult indicates he should place cubes in the mug.

00:07:17.860 --> 00:07:23.860
Child sits at the table with his thumb in his mouth. Initially there are no objects on the table, then a small glass jar is placed in front of him.

00:07:33.136 --> 00:07:39.136
The shape-board appears again and the boy is given the circle, which he fits into the correct location.

00:07:49.136 --> 00:07:55.136
The ring with string attached appears and the bell along with it. The toddler handles each object as well as the two together.

00:08:47.369 --> 00:08:57.836
He leans back in this chair and shakes the bell while facing the wall behind him.
While he is facing away, the table is removed.

00:09:00.436 --> 00:09:10.436
The child is shown walking in a circle with adults standing nearby.

00:09:10.436 --> 00:09:16.336
The six year old child is dressed and sitting at the table again.

00:09:16.336 --> 00:09:22.336
Again cubes and other objects are placed in front of him and his reactions observed. He immediately places one cube in his mouth.

00:09:36.136 --> 00:09:42.136
He continues placing cubes in his mouth, sometime removing them himself, or having them removed by the adult.

00:10:03.536 --> 00:10:09.536
The small glass jar is placed before him, and he raises it to his mouth as if to drink. When the adult discourages him, he seems agitated for a moment.

00:10:23.736 --> 00:10:29.736
The bell and then the ring appear and he plays with them. Then the shape-board again. He raises the objects to his mouth.

00:10:48.336 --> 00:10:54.336
He seems to have more trouble placing the circle shape in the correct opening.

00:10:58.469 --> 00:11:04.469
The boy stands up and his face is close to the camera.

00:11:04.536 --> 00:11:10.536
Film ends.

